WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.450
<i>Minamoto no Shigeyuki 
When winds send waves crashing against the rocks in vain, I recall how my own efforts were in vain</i>

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.440
<i>Echoing...</i>

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.070
<i>It keeps echoing around in my head.</i>

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.040
I love you.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.980
Do you think...

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.410
I'm made of stone or something?

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.580
Verse 24

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.580
When winds 
send waves 
crashing

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:31.260
Class 3-9 Homeroom Teacher 
Koda Yoshio

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.960
I know you said you want to 
be a high school teacher,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.250
but if the main reason for that is because 
you want to be a club advisor...

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.640
Frankly, I'm not sure you could handle 
the job with a motive like that.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.600
Teaching is a tremendously 
complex profession.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.640
Have you ever considered how difficult
 it is to deal with real people?

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.370
U-Uh...

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.250
I mean, being a teacher has made me such a 
lady-killer that female students scare me now!

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.610
Just when I thought he was giving sound advice...

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.100
Being loved and being hated 
are two sides of the same coin!

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.310
Well, you can always be a regular officer worker
even with a teaching certification.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.840
And you don't have to go to teachers college.
You could get a literature degree and then...

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.540
The Mashima 
Residence

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:10.920
I'm home.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.420
Taichi!

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:11.920
<b>Proficiency Test Results 
Class 3-1  Mashima Taichi</b>

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.050
What's the meaning of this?! 
Why aren't you number one?!

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.800
Were you slacking off on the 
first test of your third year?!

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.800
What have I always told you?

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.150
You're the type to hold things in, 
so you need to exhale constantly!

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.850
Focus on breathing everything out...

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.370
I quit the karuta club,

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.240
so the next one will be better.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.140
Huh?

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.940
<i>Mashima-kun, the president and central 
pillar of the karuta club...</i>

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.140
I've decided to quit.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.900
<i>I can't believe he quit the club.</i>

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.400
You traitor! I always knew 
you were that kind of guy!

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.090
Maybe I should concentrate 
on my studies, too...

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.600
I'm quitting, too.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.970
Why?! Why?! I'm bringing 
him back! Why, Taichi?!

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:51.950
What do we do? What do we do?

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.040
What can we do? What can we do?

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.450
<i>And this is the time of year when
new members join... What will we do?</i>

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.590
<b>Competitive Karuta Club 
Seeking New Members</b>

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.590
<b><i>Please come see Ayase Chihaya in class 3-9!</i></b>

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.600
<i>What will we...</i>

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.970
Everyo—

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.730
I'm second-year Hanano Sumire, and I'll 
be in charge of guiding all of you.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:10.230
I'd like to thank all of you first-years 
for your interest in joining.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.070
Our third-years have entrance 
exams to study for,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.860
and I'm sure some of you are beginners,

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.060
so I'll provide guidance and 
explanations of the basics.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.060
<i>When did Hanano-san become so reliable?!</i>

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.770
Why you?! I'll do the 
guiding and explaining!

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.670
Shut up, Tsukuba!

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.330
I'm quitting, too!

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.790
<i>I was sure that was what she'd say...</i>

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.350
<i>We're not even needed here.</i>

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.600
Take care of the karuta club after I quit.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.100
Please.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.670
Hara Miku     Class D

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.760
<i>And maybe because we stressed 
that we were national champions,</i>

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.930
Hashidate Sota     Class D

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.170
<i>we got a great balance of new members,
two boys and two girls!</i>

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:43.180
Namida Togo     Beginner

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.420
I'm Tamaru Midori from Class 1-5!

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.810
Tamaru Midori   Class A

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.060
You know how some people make it 
to Class A on sheer momentum?

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.330
I guess that's what I did!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.300
<i>The Tamaru sister?!</i>

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.050
Oh, I don't have much experience, 
but I'm in Class A!

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.550
<i>What?! At our school?!</i>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.460
I love...

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.120
the fingernails that you never grow out...

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:07.340
I love... I love... I love...

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.960
I can't play karuta.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.500
All hundred cards

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.660
look pitch-black to me.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.180
<i>When winds send waves crashing...</i>

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.080
Mr. F-Fukasaku...

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:46.940
Yes?

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.250
Mr. Fukasaku... Th-The "When winds send" poem...

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.400
The one by Minamoto no Shigeyuki?

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.250
Y-Yes. That poem...

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:03.760
<i>Minamoto no Shigeyuki 
When winds send waves crashing against the rocks in vain, I recall how my own efforts were in vain</i>

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.300
I-I...

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.770
I...

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.910
was the rock.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:10.150
I was the rock, and I... 
c-crushed them into pieces.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.150
Taichi's feelings... all these years...

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.970
All that time, I... I...

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.920
"When the winds are at their strongest,

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:27.410
the waves crash into the rocks, 
only to fall apart themselves.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:31.510
Just like those waves, my own heart
is in danger of breaking apart,

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:34.410
as I continue to pine endlessly for you."

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.960
The Hundred Poets are truly 
remarkable, aren't they?

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:41.500
Huh?

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.010
They give you the words, 
the metaphors, to express yourself.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.430
I thought it was the coming of spring

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.840
that made you seem so blurry 
around the edges of late.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.850
You seem about to fall 
apart yourself, but...

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.800
perhaps the Hundred Poets have 
been holding you together.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:04.870
Oh, dear...

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.360
Thank you.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.370
Essential Modern &
 Classical Literature
Problems 2013

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.370
B-But... Mr. Fukasaku...

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.640
I'm scared of karuta now...

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.940
I-I can't play!

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.900
Learn something.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.180
It doesn't matter what.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.740
Just learn something.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.880
Your aptitude test results 
will come back soon.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.770
Tomorrow will be the opening 
ceremony and orientation for...

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.610
Don't worry. We have a great 
med school placement course.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:41.610
Squee!

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:44.060
Hi. Taking the entry test today?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:44.920
Uh, yeah.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.560
Me, too. So we'll have
the same orientation. Literature?

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.080
Science.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.000
I heard he's applying to med school.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.040
What branch of medicine?

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.800
They're so attentive to lesson schedules here.
It makes it even harder to choose.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:55.940
English Grammar B...

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.420
I want to go for a high-level class.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.550
Yeah? Wow!

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.940
<i>Nobody here's talking about</i>

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.340
Isn't the break room here gorgeous?

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.350
<i>stuff like school clubs</i>

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:04.450
<i>or karuta.</i>

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.020
Over here, sir!

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.390
Me, too!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.420
Mr. Suo!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.480
Huh?

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:20.880
Are you...

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.130
in Class A?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:29.910
Impassionate gods have never seen
 the red that is the Tatsuta River

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.370
<b>Fukui Prefecture 
Awara City</b>

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.370
Fujioka East High School

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.920
Let's see... You want to 
start a karuta club?

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.530
You can only start a club if you 
have at least five members.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:45.170
<b>Jeez!</b>

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.670
Man, how did I know you would say that?

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.070
It happens in manga all the time!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.170
You just won't get any funding

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:45.170
But you can still enter tournaments 
with just the three of you.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.220
That's too lax.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:52.680
<b>Matsubayashi Shun (16) 
Older brother, born in April 
Class B</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.540
I know we have the right to enter 
the high school championship,

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.670
but we can't be so lax about it.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:59.180
Matsubayashi Hiro (15) 
Younger brother, born in March 
Class B

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:54.740
I think it'd be fine.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.450
There were only four schools in 
the Fukui tournament last year.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.180
I bet the three of us could win.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.530
We could practice with the Nagumo Society.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.660
Arata-niichan would be able to concentrate 
on individual tournaments, too.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.160
Yeah, since your main focus is 
individual tournaments,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.690
and the Master match.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.410
Who's entering the Hyogo 
and Sagamino tournaments?

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.390
Who's going to Hiroshima in May?

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:21.190
There's so much to do. I might 
miss the Fukui tournament.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.830
I have to handle the administrative side.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.920
You can't! Nagumo has to win 
all the local tournaments!

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.740
I'll take over as administrator for Kyoto!

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:32.150
Make sure you enter whatever 
tournaments you can, Arata.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:35.770
I'll do my best as an administrator for 
the high school championship again.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:40.360
You really don't have a very long time
to be just a karuta player.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.020
I've played long enough to know.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.480
<b>Awaraonsen Station</b>

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.890
<i>So do everything you want to do now.</i>

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.810
<i>I have people protecting me,</i>

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.900
<i>helping me.</i>

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.610
Don't say that you're not 
interested in teams!

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.650
Huh? Arata-niichan?

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.680
Sorry to interrupt your lunch.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:08.180
I'm Wataya Arata from Class 3-2.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:12.330
I'm here to recruit members for 
our competitive karuta club.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.630
Huh?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.910
We're still an association for now,

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.130
but we're seeking members to 
participate in team matches.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.580
Anyone who did their best to memorize 
the hundred poems as a kid,

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.890
anyone who ever took a card at a school 
tournament and had fun doing it...

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.940
If you work hard for the next three months,

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.490
you'll be able to compete 
with Class A players.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.720
I want to build a karuta club
that can play to win

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.900
at the high school championship 
at the end of July.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:41.210
You can talk to Matsubayashi Shun
for more details.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.810
Huh? Me?!

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:46.870
Excuse me!

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.500
Now he's gone to Class 2.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:49.340
He's going all-out.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.860
A national championship, though?

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.780
I don't know...

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:52.880
Not possible.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.760
I-It <i>is</i> possible!

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.850
The winner last year was a Tokyo school

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.290
whose karuta club had only 
been active for two years!

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.210
I was in a karuta society 
when I was little.

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:03.090
Me, too!

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.400
I'm a ranked player.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.410
That third-year was kind of hot, wasn't he?

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.750
<i>There are people here who've played.</i>

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:10.190
<i>But I didn't expect Arata-niichan
to be so serious about this...</i>

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.470
Was that Wataya?

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.110
What the heck is he doing?

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.130
He was trying to recruit 
people last year, too.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:16.980
<i>The third-year classrooms are tough...</i>

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.660
<i>Too tough for me.</i>

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.370
What are you doing, Arata? 
And now, of all times?

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:22.920
Yuu...

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.790
You're a third-year now. You don't 
have time to start a new club.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.790
You expect to find members to 
play in team tournaments <i>now</i>?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.710
I don't know.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:36.290
But right now...

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:39.290
I feel like I have to build a team.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.600
When my grandpa was still alive,

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:48.600
you helped us out a lot, remember?

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.880
To me, we were a team.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.680
Thanks, Yuu.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:58.840
<i>A team...</i>

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.320
What others have done for me...

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.230
<i>A team...</i>

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.320
And what I want to do...

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.530
If...

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.600
If you don't get anyone else, I'll joi—

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.120
A-Any of you have the 
hundred poems memorized?

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.520
I-I do.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:22.950
I think so.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.570
Any of you know the unique syllables?

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:25.340
I do!

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:26.020
I think so!

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:28.520
A-Any of you love karuta?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.870
Uh...

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:34.240
I-I'm not sure, but you 
really seem to love it.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.750
We already have people wanting to join?!

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.900
Crap! It'll be a battle to 
decide who the starters are!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.830
<i>I have to gather the wind toward me.</i>

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.530
<i>Like Chihaya and Taichi did.</i>

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:48.360
<i>I can do this, too.</i>

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.580
<b>Fukui Prefectural Fujioka East High School</b>

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:50.780
<i>This is Fukui, after all.</i>

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:55.550
<b>So you started a karuta club? 
Now?</b>

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.880
I went ahead and arranged some 
practice matches for you!

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.550
What?

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:56.920
Wataya...

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.930
What the heck kind of 
connections do you have?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.890
May

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.890
Shizuoka Prefecture 
Fujisaki High School

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:05.620
Thank you for letting us participate in 
this joint practice with you today!

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:08.520
We're the Fukui Prefectural Fujioka 
East High School Karuta Club,

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:10.890
Worn out from driving for four hours

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.890
Don't fall asleep

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.900
and I'm third-year Wataya Arata!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.560
Wow, so that's Wataya Arata?

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.540
I saw him on Nico!

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:14.110
So that's him?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.760
He's crazy good, right?

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.630
Welcome, Wataya-kun.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:20.410
We'll be sure take a real
close look at your game today.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.170
Coach Sakurazawa...

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.270
Sorry to impose when regional 
preliminaries are coming up.

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:27.750
It's all right. We do this often.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.410
The kids from Hokuo in Tokyo 
were here just last week.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:36.770
Speaking of which, you're friends with
the kids in Mizusawa's club, aren't you?

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:38.040
Oh... I am.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.610
Did you hear, then?

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.920
One of the Hokuo kids told me...

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:46.430
<b>Salute</b>

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:46.440
With Ayase and Mashima gone,
Mizusawa's karuta club is no match for us!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:50.650
Mashima-kun and Ayase-san 
quit their karuta club.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:53.890
<i>Chihaya and Taichi...</i>

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.390
<i>quit the karuta club?</i>

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:01.080
<i>That can't be right... Those two quit?</i>

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.750
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:04.530
Excuse me...

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.240
Could you place your cards, please?

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.240
Oh... Sorry.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.490
<i>Focus. I'm playing a match.</i>

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.500
<i>I can tell just by looking at her layout</i>

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.010
<i>that she's confident in her game sense.</i>

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.510
<i>So the flower has wilted...</i>

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.890
<i>For the cold nights...</i>

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:23.680
<i>She's fast.</i>

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.970
<i>The two multi-syllable "For you, I"
cards are still in play,</i>

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.600
<i>but she didn't even hesitate.</i>

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.760
<i>She really is confident.</i>

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:33.530
<i>Right.</i>

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:35.910
<i>Let's do this just like always.</i>

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.610
All right, Rion! Two in a row!
That's the way!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.980
Okay, guys, we'll get the next 
one, too! Ride this wave!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.320
Don't feel bad, Motoki!

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:42.990
You didn't get two in a row...

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:42.980
What?

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.780
All right, we're doing great, guys!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.610
Keep taking cards, one at a time! Fight!

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:47.990
Fight!

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:53.960
Rain, Silent, Look, Swift, Feel sorrow, 
Would this, Would the, Since I, After I...

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.630
<i>Rain takes longer...</i>

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.640
<i>Stop. I need to focus.</i>

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.200
<i>Just like always...</i>

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:04.460
Yay! You're awesome, Rion!

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:02.970
<b>Yay!</b>

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:06.410
<i>A house left to the weeds...</i>

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.960
Fujisaki really is strong, huh?

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:17.350
Matsubayashi Hiro        Matsubayashi Shun        Mochizuki Chiemi        Yamamoto Risa 
Won by 2 cards                 Lost by 8 cards            Lost by 15 cards             Lost by 13 cards

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.190
And we don't have much experience 
with actual matches.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:15.590
Even Matsubayashi-kun lost, though.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:17.640
And he's a Class B Nagumo Society member.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.980
I lost to Cheers...

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:18.990
Arata-niichan...

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.070
Wataya Arata 
Won by 7 cards

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:21.080
What should we do in the afternoon?

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:24.230
<i>Is it true that they quit?</i>

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:27.660
<b>Compose Message 
To: Mashima Taichi, Ayase Chihaya 
Subject: I started a karuta club</b>

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:27.020
<i>I need to at least find that out for sure.</i>

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.070
<i>If it's true, that would mean
they're feeling really lost right now.</i>

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:33.080
<i>Chihaya and Taichi both.</i>

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.740
Cheers, Wataya-kun!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:38.710
<b>Damn it!</b>

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:38.710
<i>His karuta is surprisingly 
aggressive and heavy.</i>

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.710
<b>Nnngh</b>

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.960
<b>Nnnngh</b>

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:42.960
Okay...

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:44.550
Okay! One card!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.590
Let's take one card at a time!

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.760
<i>You need to be louder, Rion.</i>

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.890
<i>It looks like we'll manage, though.</i>

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:59.810
<i>Unfortunately, Fujisaki currently lacks students
who have both talent and leadership.</i>

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.250
<i>Rion is better at karuta,</i>

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:04.850
<i>but Cheers has better leadership ability.</i>

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.860
<b>That's why I'm president!</b>

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.950
<i>If there's no one who can keep 
an eye on the team as a whole</i>

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.180
<i>while also playing great karuta,</i>

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:12.240
<i>then we need to have double leaders.</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:17.370
<b>Nnnnnnngh</b>

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:15.380
<i>To face excessively strong 
players like Wataya-kun,</i>

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.380
<i>one should be an egoist
who prioritizes to winning,</i>

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.470
Miyagawa-san, good job taking that one!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.010
<i>while the other should be a leader 
who'll call out loudly to the others.</i>

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:21.000
Akira-kun, you'll get the next one!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.000
<b>Not that she's doing that...</b>

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:26.500
<i>Mizusawa was a team with an extreme 
egoist and an extreme leader.</i>

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.550
<i>I'm not that kid from Hokuo...</i>

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.540
I'm Retro!

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:29.640
<b>I'm Retro!</b>

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:32.390
<i>But I wonder how Mizusawa will fare
without the two of them.</i>

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.890
Thank you for the game.

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:36.980
I lost... Wataya-kun was too good...

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:37.890
Hyuga Yoshihiko 
Lost by 12 cards

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:40.940
<b>Ugh...</b>

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:39.020
Cheers-senpai pulled his own hair so 
much, it went back to being straight.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.940
Don't worry. He'll curl 
it back up soon enough.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.570
All of us except Arata-niichan 
got clobbered!

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:47.440
Mochizuki Chiemi  Tsuchiya Kenichi  Matsubayashi Hiro  Matsubayashi Shun
Lost by 10 cards      Lost by 15 cards     Lost by 5 cards       Lost by 7 cards

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:46.160
<i>H-How?</i>

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.680
<i>I'm not surprised about the rest,</i>

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.830
<i>but Shun and Hiro are good 
enough to be in Class A.</i>

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:53.990
Miyagawa-san, what was the 
main problem in your match?

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.990
<i>Yet they went down so easily...</i>

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:57.450
I didn't memorize well enough, which slowed 
my attacks on the opponent's side.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.430
And you, Kawashima-kun?

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.350
My double fault halfway 
through messed me up.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.940
What messed you up was failing 
to move on from it.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:03.890
Hyuga-kun?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:05.720
He went to curl his hair.

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:06.580
Is he stupid?

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:10.200
All of you, take notes on this 
for your future selves.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.210
The third match will begin 
in fifteen minutes.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:12.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.620
<i>An adviser who gives solid guidance...</i>

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.480
<i>That's not all, though.</i>

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.970
<i>They're taking notes on other 
players' shortcomings.</i>

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:20.990
Sorry I'm late!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:21.850
<b>Curly</b>

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:21.840
Are you stupid?

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:26.870
It's on you to make sure that we don't 
lose a single match next summer.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:30.750
<i>After Coach Sakurazawa gave me
that vote of confidence,</i>

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:33.240
<i>I'm stuck sharing responsibility with Cheers...</i>

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:34.490
Hey.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.980
Did you learn anything from 
your match with Wataya-kun?

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.580
Nope, nothing. I'm not good enough 
to get anything like that from him.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.930
But we can still win as a club.

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:44.060
We'll all win this next one! Cheers!

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:45.030
Right!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.630
Third Match

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:53.140
<i>Coach Sakurazawa keeps putting 
me up against third-years.</i>

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.690
<i>I'm the only third-year in Fujioka East's club.</i>

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:00.610
<i>It's my job to keep an eye on 
the others and encourage them.</i>

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:03.050
<i>Should I talk to them?</i>

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.130
<i>I've never tried rallying cries before...</i>

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.440
<b>Let's go? 
Let's do this?</b>

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.460
<i>What should I say?</i>

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:09.580
<i>Can I even do it when I never have before?</i>

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:10.610
<b>Ahem</b>

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:12.460
<i>The storm blasts autumn leaves...</i>

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:14.290
<i>If I beat Wataya-kun,</i>

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.400
<i>it would be the best boost 
I could give this team.</i>

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.400
<i>I have to focus on winning!</i>

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.060
<i>When up against someone 
with good game sense,</i>

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:26.360
<i>in a way, it comes down to speed.</i>

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.290
<i>I need to focus, and yet...</i>

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:30.220
<i>Rallying cries?</i>

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.210
<i>I never asked to be treated colder than
 the winds of Mount Hatsuse</i>

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:31.940
<i>Watching my team?</i>

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.740
<i>How much attention can 
I afford to give them?</i>

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.300
<i>If I lose too, it won't even matter.</i>

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.670
W-We lost that one, but we'll get 'em next time!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.920
Huh? Hiro, are you talking to yourself?

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:43.980
Huh? Huh?

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:46.430
<i>That was a rallying cry?!</i>

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.310
<i>No one could tell! If you're 
gonna do that, be louder!</i>

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:51.970
<i>Oh, right...</i>

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:55.120
<i>These guys are thinking about the team, too.</i>

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:59.080
<i>I thought I needed to do something,
but I was wrong.</i>

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.330
<i>Okay...</i>

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:05.480
I'm not used to talking in a match, 
but I'm going to practice now.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.350
Fujioka East, let's talk to each other!

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:10.160
Right!

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:10.600
Y-Yeah!

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:10.860
Let's do it!

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:10.730
O-Okay!

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.090
<i>They're all over the place.</i>

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Wataya-kun's not 
very loud, either</b>

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.620
Sorry, we were all over the place,
so can we try again?

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:20.100
<b>You're doing it over?</b>

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.180
We'll come together on "All right."

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.200
"All right"?

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.110
That's the go-to for stuff like this, right?

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:23.490
Let's do this, Fujioka East!

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:25.100
Right!

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.370
<i>Oh, it kinda feels like we're a team.</i>

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.690
<b>I told them to use "All right"...</b>

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:31.600
<i>But talking to each other is just 
one of the things we need.</i>

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.060
<i>There are lots more things that 
are important for a team.</i>

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.170
<i>We'll have to learn how to 
stretch before matches, too.</i>

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:40.070
<i>He's even more sincere about 
this than I realized.</i>

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.260
<i>He's good enough to be considered 
the strongest high school player,</i>

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:47.840
<i>but he's reverting to a beginner's 
perspective in order to play as a team.</i>

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.990
<i>Why go that far to play in team matches?</i>

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:53.810
<i>It's the Master match you 
should be working toward.</i>

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.500
<i>Why?</i>

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.300
<i>There's so much more</i>

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.800
<i>that I need to learn to help this team.</i>

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:11.140
We want to thank all of you at 
Fujisaki for letting us join you.

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:13.160
We've learned a lot from this.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:15.930
Let's face off again at the nationals.

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.710
Coach Sakurazawa, we brought this for you.

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:19.620
We wish you the best
at your regional preliminary.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:22.180
Fujisaki really is a good team!

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.500
<b>They really do have 50 members!</b>

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:24.180
They have a good coach, above all!

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:25.500
I agree with that!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.210
<i>I need to start with rallying cries.</i>

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.700
<i>They can change the flow of a match.</i>

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:34.250
<i>Then there's our team composition, 
deciding our order...</i>

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.460
<i>These are all things I've 
never thought about before.</i>

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.730
<i>I'm glad we came to Shizuoka.</i>

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.740
<i>That's the kind of thing 
I need to say to them!</i>

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:44.480
E-Everyone...

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:53.100
<i>Was Mizusawa like this at first, too?</i>

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:56.980
<i>And they beat Fujisaki like that?</i>

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:00.630
<i>That's hard to believe. 
How did they practice?</i>

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:05.730
<i>That's an incredible thing, Taichi, Chihaya.</i>

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.760
<i>They quit their karuta club.</i>

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.300
<i>What happened?</i>

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:14.650
<i>What happened?</i>

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.320
<i>What happened?</i>

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:20.450
<i>Why am I always</i>

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:22.230
<i>so far away?</i>

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:24.580
No! Don't you fall asleep 
on me too, Wataya!

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:25.760
Don't leave me alone!

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:26.990
I'm awake!

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:32.470
<i>Why a team?</i>

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.840
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:38.130
<i>But I feel like I have to build a team.</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.800
Why didn't you wake us up, Mr. Kanno?!

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:48.060
We almost missed it!

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.740
You already saw it on the way here.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.110
But the sunset's different!

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.120
It's so pretty!

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:52.480
And red!

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:54.180
Did you get a picture? Send it to me!

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.970
I gotta show my parents!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:03.180
Look, Arata. These are my teammates. 
Come watch us at Omi Jingu! -Chihaya

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:02.490
<i>I was pretty late starting my team.</i>

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:07.100
<i>I have to return what Chihaya 
and Taichi gave to me.</i>

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:12.530
<i>I want to see the same 
scenery with them again.</i>

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:17.900
<b>Impassionate gods have never seen the red that is the Tatsuta River
 Like a boatsman adrift at the mouth of the Yura, I do not know where this love will take me</b>

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:20.410
<i>Ayase is in the library on a day off?</i>

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.400
<b>Anxious</b>

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.780
<b>Anxious

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.780
<b>Ancient Civilizations and the Universe</b>

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:22.790
<i>I'm so worried, I can't watch!</i>

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:28.800
She has more power than
she knows what to do with.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.960
<b>Whoa... Bottoms up...</b>

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:33.460
<b>Gasp</b>

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:36.140
Wrong pipe.

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:37.090
Yep.

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.480
<i>It's not enough.</i>

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.790
<i>No matter how much I drink...</i>

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.740
<i>No matter how much I study...</i>

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.360
<i>Suddenly, like an explosion,</i>

00:20:56.360 --> 00:21:00.700
<i>the words Taichi said to me in 
our first year came back to me.</i>

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.240
Arata will come back someday for sure.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.360
Let's get stronger and wait for his return.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:07.530
<b>New Message

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:07.530
Hope to see you at Omi Jingu

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:10.240
<b>New Message

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:14.750
What's wrong?

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:16.630
Nothing.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:20.500
I'm coming.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:25.760
Wataya Arata 
To: Mashima Taichi, Ayase Chihaya 
Subject: I made a karuta club 
Body: Hope to see you at Omi Jingu

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.310
<i>Taichi will come back someday for sure.</i>

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:26.870
<i>Let's get stronger and wait for his return.</i>

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:34.140
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>
